# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets — the reason this repository can be public.
# The ENTSO-E token belongs in .env, which is never committed.
# Commit .env.example instead, with empty values, so the required keys are documented.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
secrets.yaml

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Data — never committed. Pulls are reproducible from src/data.py, and ENTSO-E
# data carries its own reuse terms. Keep the directory structure via .gitkeep.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Note the pattern:  git never descends into an excluded *directory*, so a
# negation inside one can never fire.  `data/` would therefore swallow the
# .gitkeep files and a clean clone would come up with no data/ skeleton at all.
# Excluding the *contents* instead keeps the re-includes below working.
data/**
# Re-include the directories themselves, so git descends into them...
!data/**/
# ...and the markers that keep the skeleton alive on a clean clone.
!data/**/.gitkeep
*.parquet
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Model artefacts and experiment tracking
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
mlruns/
mlartifacts/
models/
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.onnx

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated outputs — figures are regenerated by the pipeline.
# Exception: figures referenced by the README are committed deliberately.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
reports/figures/*
!reports/figures/.gitkeep
!reports/figures/README_*.png

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Python
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# Environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Testing and type checking
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Personal study notes — deliberately out of the repository.
# docs/learnings.md is written for one reader and grows every session. The work
# log is the committed record of what was done; this is the record of what was
# understood, and it stays local.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
docs/learnings.md

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editors and OS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Same rule as data/ above: excluding the directory would make the negation
# below unreachable, because git never descends into an excluded directory.
# Exclude the contents instead, so the shared interpreter setting can be
# committed while personal editor state stays out.
.vscode/*
# Shared project configuration, listed one by one rather than by a wildcard:
# settings.json pins the interpreter, tasks.json is the command menu. Everything
# else in .vscode is personal state and stays out.
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Docker and logs (from stage 5 onwards)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
